        "excerpt": "<details open>\n\ncommon, grammar: add recursive depth limit, make it a requirement (#31153)\n\n* common, grammar: add recursive depth limit, make it a requirement\n\n* catch more recursive functions\n\n* common : tidy up peg parser changes\n\n* grammar : reject candidates in a loop, without a depth limit\n\nThe depth limit in llama_grammar_reject_candidates_for_stack counted\nthe code points of a vocab token, so any token of 256 chars or more\nwas always rejected under a grammar, such as the 512-space token of\nGLM-4.7-Flash or the long space tokens of Laguna-S-2.1.\n\nThe rejection now walks the code points with its own stack of levels\ninstead of recursing: there is no limit and no stack risk, whatever\nthe length of a token from the GGUF, and the masks match master.\n\n* grammar : track rejected candidates as indices into the input\n\nAt a given code point a candidate only differs from its input by the\nposition of its code point pointer, so the levels now carry indices\ninto the input candidates instead of copies. The first level needs no\nspecial case and the rejects map back to the input directly.\n\nGrammar sampling gets faster than master on GLM-4.7, Laguna, Qwen3.6\nand gemma-4 with the json, list an",
